{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1780072419,"nonce":"sZBpYniUU3N0suV/MBgmYyzULiY=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABDy-HI86_liC4"},"target":"56173682cc1fc650e24551ffed44201e8185306000d203b0c4fe5128ba8fdc90","message":"## Purpose\n\nFirst on-water run with the **graded sea-surface costmap** ([perception #22](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/22) / PR [#25](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/25), merged 2026-05-29). This came directly out of the #186 observation: a red buoy visible in the segmentation image that never registered on the costmap.\n\n**What changed (perception):** the costmap now accumulates *graded* per-pixel softmax log-odds (prior-shifted at `obstacle_prob_min`) instead of a hard argmax + flat hit/miss + binary LETHAL. Weak-but-persistent obstacles now bank positive evidence and mark; output is a graded cost ramp (soft `1..252` + LETHAL `254`) instead of lethal-only. All knobs are runtime-tunable.\n\n**What did NOT change:** the reflex **Collision Monitor** ([#170](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/170)) is untouched. Avoidance comes from (a) the **global planner** routing around costs and (b) the reflex monitor — the controller (`CrabbingPathFollower`) is a PID path-tracker and ignores costmap cost.\n\n## Must-verify this deployment\n\n- [ ] **The #186 fix** — aim at a dim / low-contrast buoy (the kind that showed red in the segmentation image but never marked). Confirm it now appears on the costmap (rviz), and cross-check the segmentation image still shows red there.\n- [ ] **No regression on strong obstacles** — clearly-visible buoys / docks still mark LETHAL.\n- [ ] **Graded gradient is visible** — rviz shows a soft cost ramp around uncertain areas, not just binary lethal blobs.\n- [ ] **Reflex still stops** — the Collision Monitor still halts the boat for a near obstacle (unchanged path; confirm no regression).\n- [ ] **Global route bends around marks** — with an obstacle marked, the planned global path routes around it.\n- [ ] **Recovery is reasonable** — an area that read clear water, then gets a real obstacle, re-marks within a few seconds (asymmetric clamp).\n- [ ] **No false positives from glare / reflection** — reddish water / sun glint should not mark obstacle. If it does, raise `obstacle_prob_min`.\n\n## ⚠️ Watch out for (most likely surprises)\n\n1. **Over-conservative routing — inflation × more-lethal cells.** The global costmap uses `inflation_radius: 150 m` (`cost_scaling_factor: 0.05`), so every LETHAL cell inflates a 150 m standoff bubble. Pre-#22 only strong buoys marked lethal; **now weak buoys mark too** → in a buoy field the planner may route much wider or refuse gaps. **#1 thing to watch.** Lever is config-side (`inflation_radius` / `cost_scaling_factor` in `seafloor_echoboat_project11` `nav2_params.base.yaml`), not perception.\n2. **Aggressive cost weighting.** `SmacPlannerHybrid.cost_penalty: 10.0` is high → even low-confidence *soft* costs will deflect the global route. If routes swing wide around faint stuff, raise `free_threshold` (emit less soft cost) or lower `cost_penalty` (config-side).\n3. **Sensitivity vs false positives.** `obstacle_prob_min` is the dial: lower → catches fainter buoys but more false marks; higher → conservative.\n\n## 🔧 Runtime tuning (no rebuild — tune on the water)\n\nAll on the **local_costmap** `sea_surface_layer`. **Confirm the node name on the live stack first — don't guess** (a wrong name silently sets nothing): `ros2 node list | grep -i costmap`. Then e.g.:\n```bash\n# adjust namespace/node to match `ros2 node list`\nros2 param set /bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap sea_surface_layer.obstacle_prob_min 0.30\n```\n\n| Param | Default | Effect |\n|-------|---------|--------|\n| `obstacle_prob_min` | 0.35 | **Primary dial.** Min P(obstacle) for a pixel to count; lower = more sensitive to dim buoys (more false marks), higher = conservative |\n| `max_evidence_step` | 0.85 | Per-frame evidence cap (flicker rejection; ~2 frames to lethal at default) |\n| `lethal_threshold` | 1.0 | Log-odds at/above which a cell is LETHAL |\n| `free_threshold` | 0.0 | Log-odds at/below which a cell has no opinion; between this and lethal → soft cost ramp |\n| `clear_floor` | −2.0 | Lower clamp; how fast a cleared cell can re-mark (recovery) |\n| `obstacle_clamp` | 5.0 | Upper clamp; obstacle persistence |\n| `decay_half_life_s` | 30.0 | Unobserved-evidence half-life |\n\nConstraints (a `param set` violating these is rejected, layer keeps prior value): `clear_floor ≤ free_threshold \u003c lethal_threshold ≤ obstacle_clamp`; `obstacle_prob_min ∈ (0,1)`; `max_evidence_step \u003e 0`.\n\nNote which values worked, per conditions (lighting, sea state) — these feed the durable config defaults. Bag a representative run (segmentation + costmap + plan) for offline A/B if anything looks off.\n\n## Operators\n\n- Roland + Claude Code Agent (Claude Opus 4.8, 1M context)\n\n## Hosts in use\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub)\n- **mercat** — boat-side Windows / QINSy host (if a survey phase is reached)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Date TBD** — set the title date when the deployment firms up.\n- Standing next-deployment scope folds in here too; cross-link items as they land.\n- Config-side tuning lives in `seafloor_echoboat_project11` (`nav2_params.base.yaml`) and the BizzyBoat overlay in this repo (`bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`).\n\n## Logs\n\n- Per-host under `docs/logs/2026/` once scheduled (`YYYY-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md`).\n- [dev log](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-29_dev_logs.md)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1780069647,"nonce":"PVyLaaSwtiHV2WeSE6Qjb2xY6Mk=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDy-HI88AAAAGFLZCyA"},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1780069648,"nonce":"ITcoe/s/nKFd7I6p0awzJjKfllY=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDy-HI88AAAAGFLZDQA"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780069836,"nonce":"BIugbKAleoV/U39wJjpAY7rafuA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABENIsrQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/197#issuecomment-4577176749"},"message":"## Deployment check — Collision Monitor zone overlay (CAMP) over the live bridge\n\nThe CA danger-zone overlay landed in CAMP ([rolker/camp#54](https://github.com/rolker/camp/pull/54), merged to `jazzy`): the slowdown/stop polygons now auto-display on the chart and recolor amber/red by `collision_monitor_state`. It was verified by **bag replay** of the #186 data (zones render, georeferenced, flicker SLOWDOWN↔STOP), so it's directly relevant here — operators can finally see the trigger storm that was invisible during #186.\n\n**One path bag-replay could not exercise — please confirm during this deployment:**\n\n1. **Operator station has the new CAMP build** — pull `camp` `jazzy` + rebuild on the operator host; otherwise the overlay isn't present.\n2. **Zones actually display over the *live* udp_bridge.** Bag replay used the recorded *boat-side* publisher QoS (reliable/volatile, which our overlay subscription matched). The live operator-side path is the udp_bridge **republish**, whose QoS we have not tested against the overlay. So during bring-up, confirm the slowdown/stop zones appear in CAMP and recolor while CA is active.\n3. **If the zones don't appear**, it's almost certainly a QoS mismatch, not a logic bug. Quick diagnosis at the operator station:\n   - `ros2 topic info -v \u003cbridged collision_*_polygon topic\u003e` — compare publisher vs subscriber QoS (reliability/durability).\n   - The overlay currently subscribes **reliable/volatile, depth 1**. If the bridge republishes **best-effort**, the fix is a one-line QoS change in `collision_monitor.cpp` (`setTopic`) to best_effort. Flag it and I'll turn it around.\n\nEverything else (georeferencing via dynamic `earth→bizzy/map` TF, auto-discovery, state→color routing, staleness watchdog) is verified.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780070218,"nonce":"ddeN2t3GmOv/VX8uRmIfAMh3UtI=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABENMCYw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/197#issuecomment-4577231459"},"message":"## Also landed for this run — Hover behavior fixes (#46, #48)\n\nTwo `unh_marine_navigation` fixes merged to `jazzy` today (2026-05-29). Adding\ntheir on-water watch-items here.\n\n- **[#46](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/46)** (PR [#47](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/47)) — hover no longer sticks to the first-evoked location.\n- **[#48](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/48)** (PR [#49](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/49)) — hover markers show in CAMP without a restart.\n\n**Prerequisite:** these merged to GitHub `jazzy` today — confirm the boat/sim\nbuild under test actually includes them before judging the behavior (otherwise\nyou'll see the old behavior and think the fix failed).\n\n**Validation status:** unit-tested + Copilot-reviewed, but **no sim A/B was run**\n(sim was occupied) — so this run is the first live validation. Watch closely.\n\n### Must-verify (hover)\n\n- [ ] **End-of-task hover lands where you are, not where you started.** At the end\n      of a line / task / mission, the boat should drift into a hover at its\n      *current* coasting stop point — NOT snap back to the launch point or the\n      first place it ever hovered. (This was the core #46 bug.)\n- [ ] **Re-commanded hover re-targets.** While already hovering, command a new\n      hover (override at a different lat/lon, or a new mission) — the boat should\n      move to the *new* spot. The old `clear + resend` workaround should no longer\n      be needed. Confirm it does NOT latch on the previous spot.\n- [ ] **Hover markers appear without a CAMP restart.** On a fresh launch, the green\n      hover marker sphere should render in CAMP/rviz the first time the boat\n      hovers — previously it was missing until CAMP was restarted (#48).\n\n### Watch-fors / fallback\n\n- [ ] **No hover thrash.** The same-type re-command now forces a brief hover\n      cancel+re-send on each genuine task update. Watch for any *rapid repeated*\n      cancel/re-target (thrash) — that would mean the update-time restart key is\n      bumping spuriously. (Reasoned not to, but unconfirmed without the sim A/B.)\n- [ ] **Bring-up sanity.** The new `RestartOnTaskChange` decorator fails fast if\n      `current_task_update_time` is unwired. If hover / the BT navigator fails to\n      load or run at bring-up, flag it as a wiring regression (shouldn't happen).\n- **Fallback:** if the latch reappears on the water, `clear + resend` still works\n      as the old workaround — note it and carry on.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780072009,"nonce":"OlLqyrfSZOercGeJLzXb3fUqQVo=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABENcc9w","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/197#issuecomment-4577500407"},"message":"## More landed for this run — nav behavior (secondary)\n\nThree more `unh_marine_navigation` / nav items are **merged on `jazzy`** and never\non-water-validated. **Secondary to the costmap focus** — check opportunistically;\ndon't let them pull attention off the #186 buoy-marking goal. Prerequisite (same\nas the hover items above): the boat must be rebuilt from current `jazzy`.\n\n### Trackline re-send mid-line — [unh_marine_navigation#35](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/35) (merged)\n\nThe survey-line sibling of the hover re-command above, and **class-significant**\n(students will redirect the boat mid-mission). Previously the BT latched the old\nline's path; workaround was `clear + resend`.\n\n- [ ] While the boat is following a trackline, Execute a **different** trackline →\n      it switches to the new line **without** the `clear + resend` workaround.\n      Confirm the boat actually follows the new path, not just the heartbeat updating.\n\n### Hover: no overshoot on engagement — [unh_marine_navigation#33](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/33) (merged; adds to the hover checks above)\n\nThe momentum stop-point projection (`PredictStoppingPose`) that #46 builds on;\nits on-water re-validation was deferred to the next clean-survey run.\n\n- [ ] Arriving at a hover **at speed**, the boat coasts/decelerates **into** the\n      hold point rather than overshooting and driving back to it.\n- [ ] (optional) A/B the heading mode live:\n      `ros2 param set /\u003cns\u003e/behavior_server hover.point_at_target {true,false}`\n      (confirm the node name first via `ros2 node list | grep -i behavior_server`).\n\n### If a survey phase is reached — turning limits + XTE ([PR #172](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/172) / [#124](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124) §2, [#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164))\n\nNever assessed on #173 or #186 (both buoy/CA days, no clean survey lines). **Only\nrelevant if survey lines with apron turns are run** this deployment.\n\n- [ ] Apron turns at the new planner min turning radius **1.5 m** + helm yaw cap\n      **1.0 rad/s** look controlled — no overshoot / instability at line-ends.\n- [ ] Bag a clean survey line (segmentation + costmap + `pid_state` cross-track-error)\n      for offline XTE / SE-undulation characterization (#164 — still uncharacterized;\n      prior digs were collision-test days with no sustained clean line).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1780072377,"nonce":"j4+m9lfpKPZZRelZALos6HAG5cs=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDy-HI88AAAAGFNGhsg"},"title":"Deployment 2026-05-29: validate graded sea-surface costmap (perception #22)","was":"Deployment 2026-05-29: validate graded sea-surface costmap (perception #22)"}]}